DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Prague:20261007T181000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Prague:20261007T183000
SUMMARY:PMU Event Filtering for Confidential Guests
LOCATION:Club E\, Prague Congress Centre
DESCRIPTION:Confidential Computing MC · Manali Shukla · https://lpc.event
 s/event/20/contributions/2477/\n\nPMU Event filtering is a security featur
 e that allows hypervisors to restrict which performance events guests can 
 monitor\, preventing potential side-channel attacks. However\, when using 
 hardware-acceleration PMU virtualization\, the encrypted VMSA in SEV-ES an
 d SEV-SNP creates a fundamental challenge: hypervisors cannot read or modi
 fy guest PMU states directly\, which breaks PMC filtering with hardware-ac
 celerated PMU virtualization and prevents confidential VMs from using upco
 ming AMD feature: Guest PMC Event Filtering.\n\nThis talk explores how PMC
  filtering can be restored for SEV-ES and SEV-SNP guests without weakening
  their isolation guarantees. The key idea is a cooperative model between g
 uest and hypervisor that re-establishes the hypervisor's filtering authori
 ty even when it cannot touch the guest's encrypted state directly.\n\nWe w
 ill discuss the protocol design\, implementation challenges\, and how this
  approach restores hypervisor security control over guest PMC usage in con
 fidential computing environments.
URL:https://lpc.events/event/20/contributions/2477/
END:VEVENT
